# Frontend Coding Standards

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase - `UserProfile.jsx`
- Functions: camelCase - `const handleSubmit = () => {}`
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE - `const API_BASE_URL = '...'`
- Files: Match component/function name

## Code Quality
- Keep functions small and focused
- Use meaningful variable names
- Avoid deep nesting (max 3 levels)
- Use early returns to reduce nesting
- Extract complex logic into custom hooks

## Import Rules
- **ALWAYS import at the top of the file** - Never use dynamic imports (`import()`) unless absolutely necessary for code splitting
- ✅ `import { toast } from "react-toastify";` at the top
- ❌ `import("react-toastify").then(...)` - Dynamic imports should only be used for lazy loading routes/components
- Group imports: external libraries first, then internal modules
- Use static imports for all dependencies

## React Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks
- **Do NOT use React.FC** - Use regular function declarations with TypeScript inference
  - ✅ `const Component = () => {}` (no props)
  - ✅ `const Component = ({ prop }: Props) => {}` (with props)
  - ❌ `const Component: React.FC = () => {}`
  - ❌ `const Component: React.FC<Props> = ({ prop }) => {}`
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders (use useMemo, useCallback)
- Keep state as local as possible
- Use proper key props in lists
- Avoid direct DOM manipulation

## Styling
- Use CSS modules or styled-components
- Avoid inline styles (except for dynamic styles)
- Follow BEM naming convention for CSS classes
- Keep styles scoped to components

## Performance
- Lazy load routes and heavy components
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Optimize images and assets
- Minimize bundle size
- Use code splitting

## Prohibited Patterns
- ❌ Class components (use functional components)
- ❌ React.FC type annotation (use TypeScript inference instead)
- ❌ Console.log in production (use proper logging)
- ❌ Inline styles for static styles
- ❌ Direct DOM manipulation
- ❌ Mutating state directly
- ❌ Missing key props in lists

## Required Patterns
- ✅ Functional components with hooks
- ✅ Proper error handling
- ✅ Loading states
- ✅ TypeScript or PropTypes
- ✅ Accessibility considerations
- ✅ Responsive design
